/** Which part of the source fills the 9:16 frame. x, y: centre of the crop window as a fraction of the source frame (0.5, 0.5 = centre). zoom: 1.0 = the smallest zoom that fills the output frame (no black bars); 2.0 = 2x closer. path: optional [[t, x, y], ...] keyframes (segment-local t), e.g. a face track. When present it overrides x/y. The window is always clamped inside the source, so no black edges can appear. */
